# Java Primitive Data Types

Primitive data types are the **basic built-in data types in Java**.
They store **simple values directly in memory** and are **not objects**.

Java provides 8 primitive data types, which can be grouped into four categories.

# 1️⃣ Integral Numbers

These data types store integer values without decimals.

| Type  | Size    | Wrapper Class |
| ----- | ------- | ------------- |
| byte  | 1 byte  | Byte          |
| short | 2 bytes | Short         |
| int   | 4 bytes | Integer       |
| long  | 8 bytes | Long          |

---------Important Points------------------

* `int` is the default integer type in Java.
* Any whole number written in Java is treated as int by default.
* `long` is used when the number exceeds the `int` range.
* Large `long` values must end with `L`, otherwise Java treats them as `int`.

